{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-PL-moe-planner.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-PL (campaign c2-resume, x86-main; owner Claude Opus; worker Codex) — factory component: memory planner (methodology CC)\nFactory goal (user): MoE model + system -> engine config that runs in much less memory at ~same accuracy; load time/TTFT/tok-s may change; KV-cache techniques allowed. This CC: given model stats + system profile + budget, enumerate and rank candidate configurations with PREDICTED memory/speed/quality-risk, and emit lab test definitions to MEASURE the top candidates (predictions are hypotheses; measurement decides).\nHOST NOTE: a GPU timing job is running — pure Python, no compiles, light CPU.\nInputs: model-stats/0 JSON (being built in parallel by T-MI at cc/model_inspect/; agree on fields by reading assignments/T-MI-model-inspect.md; write a small adapter so you can test with a fixture you derive by hand from facts below), host profile (cc/engine_handoff/hosts/x86-main.json) + optional resource-sample/0 (cc/resource_observe/CONTRACT.md), budget {gpu_mib, host_mib, ctx, max_quality_loss (KLD), objective decode|ttft|balanced}.\nTechnique space (llama.cpp 31288c9c6 + our patches): expert representation from available GGUFs (bf16/Q8_0/Q4_K_M/mixE4K/mixE3K/mixE2K — decisions/D009,D010,D013 have quality numbers), placement: all-GPU, `--n-cpu-moe K` (layer-granular), `--moe-cache-mib C` (engine LRU), hybrid split hot set H per layer (cc/hybrid_split), KV cache type (-ctk/-ctv f16|q8_0|q4_0, requires flash-attn -fa on), context length, ubatch/batch for TTFT.\nCost model, calibrated ONLY from our measurements (cite each): decisions/D022 (static nK and moe-cache cK: GPU MiB and decode t/s, 3 samples), D023 (shim-visible weights/KV/compute vs ~310 MiB uncounted overhead), D014/D019 (33 us per CPU-computed expert, ~15 us/layer fixed, 37.9 us/expert pinned H2D), D011 (bandwidth-bound decode; Q8_0 vs bf16 +32%), D015 (page-cache cliff when RAM < working set). Fit simple per-technique models (e.g. decode_time = gpu_time + n_cpu_layers*c1 + ...), report fit residuals, and refuse to extrapolate outside the calibrated range without a flag (mark prediction \"extrapolated\").\nDeliver cc/moe_planner/{plan.py, calibration.json (every data point with source decision + job id), PLANNER.md (methodology: decision rules, e.g. \"never use engine LRU on discrete PCIe when coverage < 60%\", \"expert precision before placement\", \"declare n_ctx: KV dominates at default ctx\", \"auto-fit is not a baseline (D023)\", \"verify mechanism engagement before timing (D024)\", with the evidence for each), test_plan.py}. CLI: `plan.py --stats S --host H --budget-gpu-mib 900 --ctx 4096 [--max-kld X] --top 5 --emit-lab-tests out.json`. Output: ranked plans with predicted gpu_mib, host_mib, decode_tps, ttft_ms, quality class, technique list, confidence (calibrated|extrapolated), and the exact llama.cpp flags.\nTests: reproduce D022 numbers within stated residuals (leave-one-out), budget feasibility logic, emitted lab tests match lab/tests/*.json schema (see bin/lab load_tests and lab/tests/match1.json).\nAllowed writes: cc/moe_planner/**, artifacts/codexPL/. 50 min. Final message: files, pytest, example plan for budget 900 MiB @ ctx 4096 on x86-main, calibration residuals, gaps.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
